  "nuclear_scope": "Both pp routines evaluated at identical T/rho/H/He3 input coordinates, retaining each routine's mass convention and screening. The F77 diagnostic extracts unchanged ENUCV/RATES from the retained source and reports pp channels only. This is a local prescription comparison, not a relaxed model or a bound on CNO/other omitted channels.",
  "f77_nuclear_driver": "      PROGRAM RATEPROBE\n      IMPLICIT DOUBLE PRECISION (A-H,O-Z)\n   10 READ(5,*,END=20) TT,RHO,X,X3\n      Z=0.02D0\n      QQ=RHO**(1.D0/3.D0)\n      CALL RATES(TT,QQ,X,X3,Z,C11,C33,C34,RC12,RC13,RC14,\n     1 RC16,FB)\n      E1=6.671D0*1.602D-6*C11*X*X\n      E3=12.860D0*1.602D-6*C33*X3*X3\n      E4=(18.982D0*(1.D0-FB)+12.50D0*FB)*1.602D-6*C34*X3\n      WRITE(6,900) E1,E3,E4,C11,C33,C34,FB\n  900 FORMAT(1P7E25.16)\n      GO TO 10\n   20 CONTINUE\n      END\n",
  "f77_source_extraction": "From SUBROUTINE ENUCV through the end of RATES, immediately before SUBROUTINE BURN. Compile driver plus these unchanged routines with gfortran -O2.",
